    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "fdae7639-d84b-3965-b9ca-6608e4df09d8",
                "word": "kyoodle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "633aaaef-4fb4-4331-b522-25a1b1431695",
                        "entry_id": "fdae7639-d84b-3965-b9ca-6608e4df09d8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "kyoodles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "afe8b369-01fc-340d-a1de-8e1fa00cc792",
                        "entry_id": "fdae7639-d84b-3965-b9ca-6608e4df09d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mutt, dog of mixed breed of little value; noisy dog."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a50bf841-d5ff-4fd7-8da7-144fac8fe428",
                                "sense_id": "afe8b369-01fc-340d-a1de-8e1fa00cc792",
                                "text": "The yelps and kyoodles had wandered home or after Rube and his idolators — all except the Widow Steger's dog, a long, strange, German sort of dog with no legs to speak of, a lonesome boyless kyoodle that had to go home early and sleep under the geranium box."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "46640559-834a-4941-a133-0f96b4ce1d22",
                                "sense_id": "afe8b369-01fc-340d-a1de-8e1fa00cc792",
                                "text": "For all the breeds and breeding on display at this most elegant of kyoodle carnivals, there is a wonderful sameness about people who go to the dogs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59d318eb-7eac-4cfc-b74e-d56c71272f57",
                                "sense_id": "afe8b369-01fc-340d-a1de-8e1fa00cc792",
                                "text": "Among other dodges that we employed to track down the border crossers, was a pack of hounds. These kyoodles worked fairly well if we put them on a track immediately after a rain, otherwise the sand was so barren of moisture it would not hold the scent for any length of time."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "57cc4769-f2d3-3e2a-8f73-7aa0f8c4ac6f",
                        "entry_id": "fdae7639-d84b-3965-b9ca-6608e4df09d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A loud, meaningless noise; howl or holler."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b74a6929-43b6-459e-8c84-c512545a07ea",
                                "sense_id": "57cc4769-f2d3-3e2a-8f73-7aa0f8c4ac6f",
                                "text": "There was a yip and kyoodle for John Brown and \"the great deeds of the past.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f03dab59-3bdb-4df7-bc44-a012587751ec",
                                "sense_id": "57cc4769-f2d3-3e2a-8f73-7aa0f8c4ac6f",
                                "text": "Liberals everywhere echoed the \"yip and kyoodle\" of the Osawatomie crowd; conservatives were aghast at Roosevelt's radicalism."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb6982ae-9b86-3040-a178-010cd6e7d8c6",
                        "entry_id": "fdae7639-d84b-3965-b9ca-6608e4df09d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large noisy collection."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac88a572-ac9c-4bf8-ae96-e911bd71e56e",
                                "sense_id": "fb6982ae-9b86-3040-a178-010cd6e7d8c6",
                                "text": "Oodles an' boodles an' kyoodles av id, Mrs. McGlaggerty!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3938c1b2-f61d-4a05-89f9-6a1bd81d37d3",
                                "sense_id": "fb6982ae-9b86-3040-a178-010cd6e7d8c6",
                                "text": "The Chrysler and me lit out like a kyoodle of pups."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa9915b0-c3d0-4f44-81a7-1dc32aecc48f",
                                "sense_id": "fb6982ae-9b86-3040-a178-010cd6e7d8c6",
                                "text": "\"I've heard of folks having ghosts,\" he said, \"but I never knew a man to have a whole kyoodle of 'em.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b4404183-0536-3d41-a701-344ea002813d",
                        "entry_id": "fdae7639-d84b-3965-b9ca-6608e4df09d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A coward or quitter; one who lacks the determination to face hardship."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4df0ab1a-5020-4c84-a421-bd7bdf4cda04",
                                "sense_id": "b4404183-0536-3d41-a701-344ea002813d",
                                "text": "If I wasn't afraid of you thinking I was a kyoodle, I'd quit the business tonight."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48a536ff-8f23-4f15-9f77-05fe51ef26f7",
                                "sense_id": "b4404183-0536-3d41-a701-344ea002813d",
                                "text": "And the reason he says that is because he's absolutely convinced that Louis has a little kyoodle in him. Tony means Louis'll quit if he's hit."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "235a00ad-d3ae-37f4-8c97-4f487462209a",
